    "tokens": 455053,
    "report": "The contact details came back hidden because the paid-stay check ignored cancelled bookings. I removed that exclusion, and the fix is committed on `main` (`be48979`). Nothing was pushed.\n\n**Cause:** `hasPaidStay` in `src/Contexts/Booking/Infrastructure/PostgresBookingQueries.ts` had `AND b.status <> 'cancelled'`. Once the traveller cancelled, the query returned false, so Messaging masked the host's phone number and the traveller's email again. Its own doc comment and ADR 55 both say a cancelled or refunded paid stay keeps lifting the hold, so the clause contradicted the rule.\n\n**Fix:** I removed that one predicate. Nothing else in what the conversation shows changed.\n\n**Test:** I added a cancellation step to the existing \"hides them … until a stay is paid\" test in `conversations.routes.e2e.spec.ts`. After the paid stay is cancelled, the host's message must still show in full. I did not run the new assertion against the old code. By reading the query, it would have failed there.\n\n**Verification:**\n- `yarn test:e2e` passed: 114 suites, 607 tests. The path argument I passed was ignored, so this ran the whole e2e suite.\n- `yarn check:conventions` and ESLint on the two changed files both passed.\n- I did not run `yarn typecheck` or `yarn test:units`.\n\n**Unclear points, decided without asking:**\n- The conventions file and ADR 55 are the reference for the intended behaviour, so I followed them over the query's wording.\n- The traveller's email in the report was not checked against the code. The fix covers any contact detail, since the same lift applies to all of them.",
